---
source: crates/cli/tests/native.rs
expression: run.stdout
---
SHA-256 checksums of files, or check them

Usage: tw sha256sum [OPTIONS] [FILE]...

Arguments:
  [FILE]...  The files; - or none for stdin

Options:
  -b, --binary          Read in binary mode: * before the name
  -c, --check           Read checksums from the FILEs and check them
      --tag             Write BSD-style lines: TAG (NAME) = HEX
  -t, --text            Read in text mode (the default)
  -z, --zero            End each line with NUL, not newline, and do not escape names
      --ignore-missing  Checking: skip files that do not exist
      --quiet           Checking: do not print OK for each file
      --status          Checking: print nothing; the exit code tells
      --strict          Checking: fail on improperly formatted lines
  -w, --warn            Checking: warn about improperly formatted lines
  -h, --help            Print help
